{"name":"Cornerstone","hex":"#e3d7bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cornerstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stone forming the base at the corner of a building.","Such a stone used ceremonially, often inscribed with the architect's and owner's names, dates and other details."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cornerstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cornerstone","blocks":[{"text":"A cornerstone is the first stone set in the construction of a masonry foundation. All other stones will be set in reference to this stone, thus determining the position of the entire structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/2018_Ko%C5%9Bci%C3%B3%C5%82_%C5%9Bw._Antoniego_w_Las%C3%B3wce_1.jpg/330px-2018_Ko%C5%9Bci%C3%B3%C5%82_%C5%9Bw._Antoniego_w_Las%C3%B3wce_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornerstone"},{"title":"Cornerstone (Styx album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cornerstone is the ninth studio album by the American rock band Styx, released in 1979. Styx's third straight multi-platinum selling album, Cornerstone was Styx's first album to earn a Grammy nomination, which was for Best Rock Performance by a Duo or Group. Like the four previous Styx albums, the band produced the album themselves. Styx recorded the album at Pumpkin Studios in Oak Lawn, Illinois."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/Styx_-_Cornerstone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornerstone_(Styx_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/DCJCC_cornerstone_ceremony.jpg/500px-DCJCC_cornerstone_ceremony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/DCJCC_cornerstone_ceremony.jpg/1280px-DCJCC_cornerstone_ceremony.jpg?utm_sou